Port of _patches/typescript/024-ls-document-symbols.patch (tsc/internal/ls/symbols.go) to tsrs.

- AfterDocumentSymbolsCallback, RegisterAfterDocumentSymbolsCallback: `tsrs_ls::{AfterDocumentSymbolsCallback,
  register_after_document_symbols_callback}` (a `fn` in a process-wide `RwLock`; registering replaces it).
  getDocumentSymbolsForChildren passes the merged symbols through it, as in Go.
- Go's callback works on `[]*lsproto.DocumentSymbol`; tsrs builds the tree as shared `DocSym`s
  (`Rc<RefCell<DocSymData>>`, turned into `lsproto::DocumentSymbol`s when the response is built), so the callback
  takes and returns `DocSym`s: `DocSym` and `DocSymData` become `pub` (re-exported from the crate root) and
  `DocSymData` gets the `detail` field of `lsproto::DocumentSymbol` (Go's `Detail`), copied by `doc_sym_to_lsp`
  (tsrs's own symbols leave it `None`, as Go's do).

